I go to the customer service counter in the store.
There is a clerk there.
I give the green shirt and the receipt to him.
He looks at the receipt.
"What is the problem?" he asks.
I explain the matter to him.
"I bought this shirt yesterday."
"But this shirt is very small."
"My size is bigger than this."
"Can I exchange this?" I ask.
He nods his head with a smile.
"Certainly, we can exchange this," he says.
"Do you have a size bigger than this for this same shirt?" I ask.
"Let me just check," he says.
He searches in the computer.
"Yes, there is a size bigger than this here," he says.
He goes inside to get that shirt.
I wait near the counter.
